{"description":"Define the control-plane protobuf schema and wire up code generation into the build.\n\nCovers the envelope with a per-message-type oneof, and the message set the MVP needs: handshake and resume, heartbeat, presence update and status change, direct message, broadcast, attachment transfer for voice notes, queue drain with positions, acknowledgement, and public-key distribution.\n\nSchema evolution matters from day one because the fleet will run mixed client versions: unknown fields must be ignored rather than rejected.","acceptanceCriteria":"1. Code generation runs as part of the build and its output is reproducible.\n2. Golden encode/decode tests cover every message type in the schema.\n3. A message carrying an unknown field decodes successfully, with the unknown field preserved rather than dropped or fatal.\n4. The schema carries an explicit version, and a version mismatch produces a clear diagnostic rather than a decode failure.\n5. The generated package has no CGO dependency."}